# config_refusal Live-degradation gate transcript — GREEN (ADDITIVE)

The red→green pin for the §18 config-key refusal seam's Live-degradation
warning. Companion to `config_refusal_red.log`.

## GREEN — the pin matches the landed R02 matrix

`warns_live_on_degraded_cells_with_the_documented_string` now iterates ONLY
the Serverless class (Lambda, Vercel, VercelFunctions, Netlify — Degraded for
Live, the F05 ruling); the new `refuses_live_on_edge_targets` asserts
Cloudflare + CloudflarePages (Edge → Unsupported per V2-E09) produce the
`AST-LIV-001` ERROR with the §18 reason ("does not support live loaders").

    $ cargo test -p oxide-fw-adapters --test config_refusal_tdd
    test refuses_live_on_static ... ok
    test refuses_live_on_edge_targets ... ok
    test refuses_search_on_edge ... ok
    test refuses_rust_fns_on_every_non_native_target ... ok
    test the_matrix_row_agrees_with_the_refusal_wiring ... ok
    test severity_split_on_a_degraded_target ... ok
    test the_seam_consults_the_matrix_not_a_private_table ... ok
    test warns_degraded_search_on_node ... ok
    test warns_live_on_degraded_cells_with_the_documented_string ... ok
    ...
    test result: ok. 17 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored

The degradation string the warning carries is still
`degradation(target, Capability::Live)` — the single source of truth — for
every Serverless target. The Edge refusal is now an honest ERROR, not a
silently-misread warning.
